DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     These interfaces may be used to convert between the local and BSM proto‐
     col domains.  The aauu__bbssmm__ttoo__ddoommaaiinn() function accepts a BSM domain,
     _b_s_m___d_o_m_a_i_n, and converts it to a local domain, such as those passed to
     socket(2), that will be stored in the integer pointed to by _l_o_c_a_l___d_o_m_a_i_n_p
     if successful.  This call will fail if the BSM domain cannot be mapped
     into a local domain, which may occur if the socket token was generated on
     another operating system.

     The aauu__ddoommaaiinn__ttoo__bbssmm() function accepts a local domain, and returns the
     BSM domain for it.  This call cannot fail, and instead returns a BSM do‐
     main indicating to a later decoder that the domain could not be encoded.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     On success, aauu__bbssmm__ttoo__ddoommaaiinn() returns 0 and a converted domain; on fail‐
     ure, it returns -1 but does not set errno(2).

